;; Authored ordered compositions of reusable blocks.
;; Depends on 1-tags.edn and 2-blocks.edn; agents are defined separately.
;;
;; A hyperdoc owns placement entities, not the referenced blocks. The same block
;; may appear in multiple hyperdocs or multiple positions in one hyperdoc.
;; Placement entities use their EDB identity; no separate UUID or author is
;; required. The hyperdoc has exactly one who/author for its creation and
;; composition; generated blocks/tags retain their own authors, not that user.
;;
;; Concrete hyperdoc types are authored native entity specs with db/ident,
;; hyperdoc-type/title, who/author, and db.entity/attrs and/or
;; db.entity/preds. Writers ensure hyperdoc/validate AND the selected type spec.
;;
;; Schema-only draft: the declared native predicates are not implemented or
;; registered. Missing callbacks must prevent successful validation.
;; Explicitly ensure edits, placement ownership/order, and affected containers;
;; component refs and type refs do not automatically ensure entity specs.
;; Preserve history. Blueprint edits do not retroactively validate documents.
[
 {:db/ident :hyperdoc-type/title
  :db/valueType :db.type/string
  :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one
  :db/doc "Nonempty human-readable name of an authored hyperdoc blueprint, for example Lesson or Homework. The same entity has a db/ident, who/author, and native entity-spec facts. Ensure hyperdoc-type/validate when authoring it."}

 {:db/ident :hyperdoc-type/required-block-types
  :db/valueType :db.type/ref
  :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many
  :db/doc "Concrete block blueprints that must each appear in at least one placement. Absence adds no required block types and does not restrict other valid types. Combine with singular-block-types to require exactly one occurrence. These ordinary refs preserve shared block blueprints."}

 {:db/ident :hyperdoc-type/singular-block-types
  :db/valueType :db.type/ref
  :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many
  :db/doc "Concrete block blueprints permitted at most once in this hyperdoc. Count placements by their referenced block's type, not distinct block identities: placing the same block twice counts twice. A type also in required-block-types must occur exactly once. Types outside this set may repeat."}

 {:db/ident :hyperdoc/id
  :db/valueType :db.type/uuid
  :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one
  :db/unique :db.unique/identity
  :db/doc "Stable identity of an authored composition of blocks, independent of its current arrangement or revision."}

 {:db/ident :hyperdoc/type
  :db/valueType :db.type/ref
  :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one
  :db/doc "Concrete authored native entity spec defining this hyperdoc's blueprint. Must satisfy hyperdoc-type/validate. This ordinary ref neither owns the shared blueprint nor automatically invokes it. Writers ensure the generic hyperdoc spec and the selected concrete spec."}

 {:db/ident :hyperdoc/placements
  :db/valueType :db.type/ref
  :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/many
  :db/isComponent true
  :db/doc "Placement entities exclusively owned by this hyperdoc. The ref collection is unordered; sort by hyperdoc-placement/index to obtain document order. Each placement references one reusable block. Component ownership retracts placements with the hyperdoc, while ordinary block refs preserve content. The future validator must enforce single ownership; isComponent alone does not."}

 {:db/ident :hyperdoc-placement/block
  :db/valueType :db.type/ref
  :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one
  :db/doc "The reusable block at this position. Ordinary ref preserves the block and its authorship when this placement or hyperdoc is removed. Validate the block against its generic and concrete blueprint specs. Editing the shared block changes its current content in every referring hyperdoc; historical interpretations require the relevant database basis."}

 {:db/ident :hyperdoc-placement/index
  :db/valueType :db.type/long
  :db/cardinality :db.cardinality/one
  :db/doc "Positive, 1-based display position, unique within the owning hyperdoc. Gaps are allowed; global uniqueness is neither required nor appropriate. This contextual order belongs to the placement, not the shared block. Its owner is found by reverse lookup of hyperdoc/placements."}

 {:db/ident :hyperdoc-type/validate
  :db.entity/attrs [:db/ident :hyperdoc-type/title :who/author]
  :db.entity/preds course-academy.generics/valid-hyperdoc-type?
  :db/doc "Strict hyperdoc-blueprint contract. The future predicate checks a nonempty title, one valid author agent, an actual native entity spec with required attrs and/or predicates, and valid concrete block-blueprint targets in both rule sets. Required and singular sets may overlap or be absent. Ensuring this spec does not revalidate existing hyperdocs."}

 {:db/ident :hyperdoc-placement/validate
  :db.entity/attrs [:hyperdoc-placement/block :hyperdoc-placement/index]
  :db.entity/preds course-academy.generics/valid-hyperdoc-placement?
  :db/doc "Requires a valid complete block, positive index, and exactly one hyperdoc owner through hyperdoc/placements. The future predicate checks index uniqueness among that owner's placements in the proposed database. The placement inherits attribution for arrangement from the hyperdoc; it does not override block/tag authors. Writers ensure the owning hyperdoc too, including after removal or reordering."}

 {:db/ident :hyperdoc/validate
  :db.entity/attrs [:hyperdoc/id :hyperdoc/type :hyperdoc/placements
                    :who/author]
  :db.entity/preds course-academy.generics/valid-hyperdoc?
  :db/doc "Strict complete-hyperdoc contract requiring identity, a concrete blueprint, at least one placement, and exactly one valid author agent. The future predicate checks the blueprint, exclusive placement ownership, positive unique indexes, complete referenced blocks/tags, and required/singular block-type counts by placement. Writers additionally ensure each referenced block's selected native spec and this hyperdoc's selected native spec for extra rules. Only the explicitly ensured specs execute; edits to shared children require ensuring affected containers. Additional metadata is allowed."}
]
